      "Real diff tools instead solve for the longest common subsequence between two texts — the largest set of lines (or characters) that appear in the same relative order in both versions — and report everything outside that shared sequence as an insertion or deletion. This correctly isolates a single inserted line as one small change, not a cascade of false positives.",
